/**
  @page examples-io-index Input/output examples
  @brief Export a field for visualization or exchange mesh files.

  @tableofcontents

  @m_footernavigation

  Choose the example according to the data being exchanged. XDMF is the
  starting point for visualizing a computed field; the mesh-format examples
  cover importing and exporting geometry.

  @section examples-io-index-xdmf Visualize a field with XDMF

  The XDMF format is recommended for visualization. It produces files
  compatible with [ParaView](https://www.paraview.org/):

  - @subpage examples-io-xdmf — Export a time-dependent vector field.

  @section examples-io-index-mesh Exchange mesh files

  Examples demonstrating mesh I/O and format conversion:

  - @subpage examples-io-mfem — Save and reload a mesh and scalar field.
  - @subpage examples-io-medit — Create a mesh, save it in MEDIT and convert it to MFEM.

  @section examples-io-index-see-also Further reading

  - @ref guides-io "I/O in Rodin" — Format selection and visualization workflows
  - @ref guides-io-xdmf "XDMF format guide"

  */
